def hipsparseSbsrsm2_solve(object handle, object dirA, object transA, object transX, int mb, int nrhs, int nnzb, object alpha, object descrA, object bsrSortedValA, object bsrSortedRowPtrA, object bsrSortedColIndA, int blockDim, object info, object B, int ldb, object X, int ldx, object policy, object pBuffer):
    r"""Sparse triangular system solve using the BSR storage format.

    ``hipsparseXbsrsm2_solve`` solves a sparse triangular linear system of a sparse
    :math:`m \times m` matrix, defined in BSR storage format, a column-oriented dense solution matrix
    :math:`X` and the column-oriented dense right-hand side matrix :math:`B` that is multiplied by :math:`\alpha`,
    such that

    .. math::

       op(A) \cdot op(X) = \alpha \cdot op(B),

    with

    .. math::

       op(A) = \left*    \begin{array}{ll}
           A,   & \text{if transA == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_NON_TRANSPOSE} \\
           A^T, & \text{if transA == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_TRANSPOSE} \\
           A^H, & \text{if transA == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_CONJUGATE_TRANSPOSE}
       \end{array}
       \right.

    ,

    .. math::

       op(B) = \left*    \begin{array}{ll}
           B,   & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_NON_TRANSPOSE} \\
           B^T, & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_TRANSPOSE} \\
           B^H, & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_CONJUGATE_TRANSPOSE}
       \end{array}
       \right.

    and

    .. math::

       op(X) = \left*    \begin{array}{ll}
           X,   & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_NON_TRANSPOSE} \\
           X^T, & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_TRANSPOSE} \\
           X^H, & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_CONJUGATE_TRANSPOSE}
       \end{array}
       \right.

    and where :math:`m = blockDim \times mb`.

    Note that, as indicated above, the operation type of both :math:`op(B)` and :math:`op(X)` is specified by the
    ``transX`` parameter and that the operation type of :math:`B` and :math:`X` must match. For example, if :math:`op(B)=B`, then
    :math:`op(X)=X`. Likewise, if :math:`op(B)=B^T`, then :math:`op(X)=X^T`.

    Given that the sparse matrix :math:`A` is a square matrix, its size is :math:`m \times m` regardless of
    whether :math:`A` is transposed or not. The size of the column-oriented dense matrices :math:`B` and :math:`X`
    depends on the value of ``transX:``

    .. math::

       op(B) = \left*    \begin{array}{ll}
           ldb \times nrhs, \text{  } ldb \ge m, & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_NON_TRANSPOSE} \\
           ldb \times m, \text{  } ldb \ge nrhs,  & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_TRANSPOSE} \\
           ldb \times m, \text{  } ldb \ge nrhs, & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_CONJUGATE_TRANSPOSE}
       \end{array}
       \right.

    and

    .. math::

       op(X) = \left*    \begin{array}{ll}
           ldb \times nrhs, \text{  } ldb \ge m, & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_NON_TRANSPOSE} \\
           ldb \times m, \text{  } ldb \ge nrhs,  & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_TRANSPOSE} \\
           ldb \times m, \text{  } ldb \ge nrhs, & \text{if transX == HIPSPARSE_OPERATION_CONJUGATE_TRANSPOSE}
       \end{array}
       \right.

