    .. math::

       A \approx LU

    where the lower triangular matrix :math:`L` and the upper triangular matrix :math:`U` are computed using:

    .. math::

       \begin{array}{ll}
           L_{ij} = \frac{1}{U_{jj}}(A_{ij} - \sum_{k=0}^{j-1}L_{ik} \times U_{kj}), & \text{if i > j} \\
           U_{ij} = (A_{ij} - \sum_{k=0}^{j-1}L_{ik} \times U_{kj}), & \text{if i <= j}
       \end{array}

    for each entry found in the CSR matrix :math:`A`.

    Computing the above incomplete :math:`LU` factorization requires three steps to complete. First,
    the user determines the size of the required temporary storage buffer by calling
    ``hipsparseScsrilu02_bufferSize`` . After this buffer size has been determined,
    the user allocates the buffer and passes it to ``hipsparseScsrilu02_analysis`` .
